-- title:
--   A module-finite overring in κ with locally principal maximal ideals
-- statement:
--   Let $C$ be a discrete valuation ring (a commutative domain satisfying `IsDiscreteValuationRing`), let $K_0$ be a field which is a $C$-algebra and a fraction field of $C$, and let $\kappa$ be a field extension of $K_0$ that is finite-dimensional over $K_0$ and separable over $K_0$, with a $C$-algebra structure making $C \to K_0 \to \kappa$ a tower. Let $A$ be any commutative ring equipped with $C$-algebra and $\kappa$-algebra structures, i.e. a $C$-algebra together with a ring homomorphism $A \to \kappa$ compatible with $C \to \kappa$ (no injectivity or finiteness is assumed of $A$). The assertion is the existence of an $A$-subalgebra $D_1$ of $\kappa$ such that: (i) $D_1$ is finite as an $A$-module; (ii) every $x \in \kappa$ that is integral over $C$ belongs to $D_1$, so $D_1$ contains the integral closure of $C$ in $\kappa$; and (iii) every maximal ideal $\mathfrak n$ of $D_1$ is locally principal in the following explicit sense: there is $t \in \mathfrak n$ such that for each $x \in \mathfrak n$ one can find $s \in D_1 \setminus \mathfrak n$ and $y \in D_1$ with $s x = t y$.
--
--   This is the standard construction of a module-finite overring, namely the $A$-algebra generated by the integral closure $\mathcal O$ of $C$ in $\kappa$ (a semilocal Dedekind, hence principal ideal, domain by Krull–Akizuki), packaged so that each maximal ideal becomes principal after inverting an element outside it. It supplies the local normalisation used in the analysis of the rings attached to the nodal annulus in the curve-theoretic part of the development, and is cited by the lemmas of the `AlgebraicCurve.NodeAnnulusEngine` development about quotients and evaluation maps.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsDiscreteValuationRing_exists_finite_locallyPrincipalOverring.lean

